# Client-safe only — never put a service_role key or database password in
# any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable. Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* values into the
# built JS bundle at build time (see lib/supabase.ts), so they are always
# visible to anyone who opens the app, by design — that's why only the
# public anon key belongs here, protected by RLS, never service_role.
#
# On Vercel: set these under Project Settings -> Environment Variables
# before the first build. Changing them later requires a new deployment
# (rebuild), not just an env var update, since they're compiled in.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
